+
+## 6. Diagnostics
+
+Run `python3 tools/rfoundry_debug.py view --section nxdn_trunk` while the channel is on a Type-C site.
+The counters describe the current follower session. Compare two readings while the control channel is on air.
+
+| Key (prefix `nxdn.trunk.`) | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `cac_ok`, `cac_fail`, `cac_dropped` | Valid CRC, failed CRC or discarded before the follower received it. A valid CRC with a mismatched RAN also increments `nxdn.ran_rejects` in the `nxdn` view |
+| `control_hz`, `listen_hz` | Configured control channel and the frequency selected by the follower. These values do not indicate synthesizer lock or useful signal strength |
+| `site_known`, `location`, `dfa`, `base`, `step` | SITE_INFO received, its location ID and frequency assignment parameters |
+| `assigns`, `assigned_chan`, `assigned_hz` | Number of voice assignments and the channel number or OFN and frequency derived from the last one (0 Hz: no usable plan) |
+| `follows`, `refusals`, `reason` | Voice assignments accepted and rejected. Last refusal 0: none, 1: no plan, 2: recent call rejoin guard, 3: frequency refused by the receiver |
+| `tx_enabled` | 1 when the follower is configured to register and request voice. Other transmit gates still apply |
